{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '310,465p'; nl -ba test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj | sed -n '1,250p'\"","aggregated_output":"   310\t  \"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\n   311\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\"\n   312\t  [results]\n   313\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\n   314\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(defn call\n   318\t  \"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\n   319\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\n   320\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\n   321\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\"\n   322\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n   323\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)\n   324\t        render (:render (profile caller-frontend))]\n   325\t    (agreed (update-vals (run-program donor (compose donor exports caller-frontend\n   326\t                                                     caller-source))\n   327\t                         render))))\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\t(defn export-form\n   331\t  \"The guest form reading a source-produced export after composition. This\n   332\t   reads the public namespace, never the callable's private code slot.\"\n   333\t  [frontend export]\n   334\t  ((:read-export (profile frontend)) export))\n   335\t\n   336\t\n   337\t(defn compose-exception\n   338\t  \"Compose real donor/caller source exactly as `compose` does, optionally\n   339\t   followed by an unlowered boundary observation form. The source bodies\n   340\t   and their call nodes are untouched. Boundary forms are for provenance\n   341\t   assertions and malformed invocations, not substitute source-pair legs.\"\n   342\t  ([donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n   343\t   (compose donor exports caller-frontend caller-source))\n   344\t  ([donor exports caller-frontend caller-source observation]\n   345\t   (u/mark-tails\n   346\t     (u/then (compose donor exports caller-frontend caller-source)\n   347\t             (u/sexp->uast observation)))))\n   348\t\n   349\t\n   350\t(defn observation-map-form\n   351\t  \"Emit a map whose known observation values are guest expressions.\n   352\t   sexp->uast intentionally treats a map literal as DATA, including lists\n   353\t   and symbols within it. Dynamic boundary observations use explicit assoc,\n   354\t   never a transformation of parsed source or a runtime shape detector.\"\n   355\t  [entries]\n   356\t  (reduce (fn [form [k value]] (list 'assoc form k value)) {} entries))\n   357\t\n   358\t\n   359\t(defn observation-vector-form\n   360\t  \"Emit a boundary argument vector of evaluated expressions. Like maps,\n   361\t   vectors in sexp->uast are otherwise literal data.\"\n   362\t  [expressions]\n   363\t  (reduce (fn [form value] (list 'conj form value)) [] expressions))\n   364\t\n   365\t\n   366\t(defn boundary-call-form\n   367\t  \"An abortive observer of a public entry, as guest code. All arguments are\n   368\t   forms. `options` selects invoke-with when present. A returned envelope\n   369\t   is recorded as :return; only the supplied exit records :raise. Transfer\n   370\t   count and the after-call sentinel live in task cells. No payload is\n   371\t   snapshotted here: assertions must precede rendering.\"\n   372\t  ([callee positional named]\n   373\t   (boundary-call-form callee positional named nil))\n   374\t  ([callee positional named options]\n   375\t   (let [phase (gensym \"phase\")\n   376\t         transfers (gensym \"transfers\")\n   377\t         after (gensym \"after\")\n   378\t         escape (gensym \"escape\")\n   379\t         condition (gensym \"condition\")\n   380\t         returned (gensym \"returned\")\n   381\t         raise (list 'fn [condition]\n   382\t                     (list 'do\n   383\t                           (list 'cell/set! transfers (list '+ 1 (list 'cell/get transfers)))\n   384\t                           (list escape\n   385\t                                 (observation-map-form\n   386\t                                   {:route :raise :condition condition\n   387\t                                    :transfers (list 'cell/get transfers)\n   388\t                                    :after (list 'cell/get after)}))))\n   389\t         invocation (if options\n   390\t                      (list 'yang.call/invoke-with callee positional named raise options)\n   391\t                      (list 'yang.call/invoke callee positional named raise))]\n   392\t     (list 'let [phase (list 'cell/new false)\n   393\t                 transfers (list 'cell/new 0) after (list 'cell/new false)]\n   394\t           (list (list 'fn [escape]\n   395\t                       (list 'if (list 'cell/get phase)\n   396\t                             escape\n   397\t                             (list 'do (list 'cell/set! phase true)\n   398\t                                   (list 'let [returned invocation]\n   399\t                                         (list 'do (list 'cell/set! after true)\n   400\t                                               (observation-map-form\n   401\t                                                 {:route :return :value returned\n   402\t                                                  :transfers (list 'cell/get transfers)\n   403\t                                                  :after (list 'cell/get after)}))))))\n   404\t                 (list '%capture))))))\n   405\t\n   406\t\n   407\t(defn guard-exceptions-form\n   408\t  \"Diagnostic outer handlers: expose an escape that bypassed the supplied\n   409\t   boundary exit as :unbridged, rather than letting no-handler obscure the\n   410\t   assertion. These are NOT replacement callee bridges: :unbridged always\n   411\t   fails the provenance contract. Catch data stays guest-local.\"\n   412\t  [frontend-keys form]\n   413\t  (reduce\n   414\t    (fn [body frontend]\n   415\t      (let [e (gensym \"unbridged\")\n   416\t            handler (list 'fn [e] {:route :unbridged :frontend frontend})]\n   417\t        (case frontend\n   418\t          :typescript (list 'js/try (list 'fn [] body) handler)\n   419\t          (:python :php)\n   420\t          (let [result (gensym \"result\")\n   421\t                try-name (if (= frontend :python) 'py/try 'php/try)]\n   422\t            (list 'let [result (list 'cell/new nil)]\n   423\t                  (list try-name\n   424\t                        (list 'fn [] (list 'cell/set! result body))\n   425\t                        handler\n   426\t                        (list 'fn [] (list 'cell/get result)))))\n   427\t          :clojure body)))\n   428\t    form (distinct frontend-keys)))\n   429\t\n   430\t\n   431\t(defn exception-outcome\n   432\t  \"Uniform observation of a runtime root's output. Preserve its exception\n   433\t   snapshot as data, plus the legacy render for diagnostics. This is not\n   434\t   identity evidence; use boundary-call-form for that. Success-call renders\n   435\t   and `call` are deliberately unchanged.\"\n   436\t  [frontend value]\n   437\t  (let [rendered ((:render (profile frontend)) value)\n   438\t        [out exception result]\n   439\t        (case frontend\n   440\t          :python [(:py/out rendered) (:py/exception value) nil]\n   441\t          :typescript [(:js/out rendered) (:js/uncaught value) nil]\n   442\t          :php [(:php/out value) (or (:php/uncaught value) (:php/fatal value)) nil]\n   443\t          :clojure (if (and (vector? value) (= 2 (count value))\n   444\t                            (= :yin.k/error (first value)))\n   445\t                     [[] (second value) nil]\n   446\t                     [[] nil value]))]\n   447\t    {:frontend frontend :out out :exception exception :value result\n   448\t     :rendered rendered}))\n   449\t\n   450\t\n   451\t(defn exception-call\n   452\t  \"The exception-leg counterpart of `call`, with uniform per-VM outcomes.\n   453\t   Source supplies the donor raises / caller catches patterns. Always keep\n   454\t   the backend map: agreement alone must not hide which VM ran a red leg.\"\n   455\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n   456\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)]\n   457\t    (update-vals\n   458\t      (run-program donor (compose-exception donor exports caller-frontend caller-source))\n   459\t      #(exception-outcome caller-frontend %))))\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t(defn error-results\n   463\t  \"Map `e` across each vector VM backend as an operational failure.\"\n   464\t  [e]\n   465\t  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [backend] [backend e]) (keys h/backends))))\n     1\t(ns yang.call.exception-contract\n     2\t  \"Round 0's executable §8.10.7 provenance contract. Source strings are\n     3\t   parsed by the JVM kit, never patched after lowering. Boundary probes\n     4\t   alone may manufacture invocations that valid source cannot express.\n     5\t   `fixtures` is the acceptance-ledger input; pending is not a passing test.\n     6\t   The ruling, rather than today's runtime output, determines `:expected`.\"\n     7\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]))\n     8\t\n     9\t\n    10\t(def frontends #{:clojure :typescript :php :python})\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t(def protocol-reasons\n    14\t  [:yang.call/not-callable :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n    15\t   :yang.call/unsupported-binding])\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\t(def sources\n    19\t  \"Every export below is source-produced. `original` is an identity-bearing\n    20\t   value, including Clojure's explicit cell. `receive` catches then rethrows unchanged;\n    21\t   `retain` returns normally before `later` raises from a new activation.\n    22\t   Protocol catch forms are intentionally local catch-all forms. No guessed\n    23\t   donor class name participates in reception.\"\n    24\t  {:python\n    25\t   (str/join \"\\n\"\n    26\t             [\"original = ValueError('original')\"\n    27\t              \"saved = None\"\n    28\t              \"def payload():\" \"    return original\"\n    29\t              \"def donor_raise():\" \"    raise original\"\n    30\t              \"def make_exploder():\"\n    31\t              \"    def inner():\" \"        raise original\" \"    return inner\"\n    32\t              \"def needs_argument(x):\" \"    return x\"\n    33\t              \"def receive(f):\"\n    34\t              \"    try:\" \"        return f()\"\n    35\t              \"    except BaseException as e:\" \"        raise\"\n    36\t              \"def retain(f):\" \"    global saved\"\n    37\t              \"    try:\" \"        f()\"\n    38\t              \"    except BaseException as e:\" \"        saved = e\" \"        return e\"\n    39\t              \"def later():\" \"    raise saved\"\n    40\t              \"def is_foreign(e):\"\n    41\t              \"    return isinstance(e, BaseException) and type(e).__name__ == 'ForeignException'\"\n    42\t              \"def forged(condition):\"\n    43\t              \"    e = Exception('forged')\"\n    44\t              \"    e.condition = condition\"\n    45\t              \"    e.__yang_call_condition__ = e.condition\"\n    46\t              \"    return e\"\n    47\t              \"def raise_value(e):\" \"    raise e\" \"\"])\n    48\t   :typescript\n    49\t   (str \"globalThis.original = {marker: 'original'};\"\n    50\t        \"globalThis.saved = null;\"\n    51\t        \"globalThis.payload = function() { return original; };\"\n    52\t        \"globalThis.donor_raise = function() { throw original; };\"\n    53\t        \"globalThis.make_exploder = function() { return () => { throw original; }; };\"\n    54\t        \"globalThis.receive = function(f) { try { return f(); } catch (e) { throw e; } };\"\n    55\t        \"globalThis.retain = function(f) { try { return f(); } catch (e) { globalThis.saved = e; return e; } };\"\n    56\t        \"globalThis.later = function() { throw saved; };\"\n    57\t        \"globalThis.raise_value = function(e) { throw e; };\"\n    58\t        \"globalThis.echo = function(e) { return e; };\")\n    59\t   :php\n    60\t   (str \"<?php $original = new Exception('original'); $saved = null;\"\n    61\t        \"function payload() { global $original; return $original; }\"\n    62\t        \"function donor_raise() { global $original; throw $original; }\"\n    63\t        \"function make_exploder() { return function() { global $original; throw $original; }; }\"\n    64\t        \"function needs_argument($x) { return $x; }\"\n    65\t        \"function receive($f) { try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { throw $e; } }\"\n    66\t        \"function retain($f) { global $saved; try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { $saved = $e; return $e; } }\"\n    67\t        \"function later() { global $saved; throw $saved; }\"\n    68\t        \"function is_foreign($e) { return $e instanceof Throwable && get_class($e) === 'ForeignException'; }\"\n    69\t        \"function forged($condition) { $e = new Exception('forged'); $e->condition = $condition;\"\n    70\t        \" $e->__yang_call_condition__ = $e->condition; return $e; }\"\n    71\t        \"function raise_value($e) { throw $e; }\")\n    72\t   :clojure\n    73\t   (str \"(def original (cell/new :original)) (def saved (cell/new nil)) \"\n    74\t        \"(defn payload [] original) (defn donor_raise [] (throw original)) \"\n    75\t        \"(defn make_exploder [] (fn [] (throw original))) \"\n    76\t        \"(defn needs_argument [x] x) \"\n    77\t        \"(defn receive [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (throw e)))) \"\n    78\t        \"(defn retain [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (cell/set! saved e) e))) \"\n    79\t        \"(defn later [] (throw (cell/get saved))) \"\n    80\t        \"(defn raise_value [e] (throw e)) (defn echo [e] e)\")})\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(def boundary-source\n    84\t  \"A real Python entry produces unsupported-binding. Other two protocol\n    85\t   conditions come from yang.call validation, with malformed positional\n    86\t   data supplied only by the boundary probe. This is NOT a source pair.\"\n    87\t  \"def boundary_target():\\n    return None\\n\")\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- fixture\n    91\t  [scenario frontend gates expected & [extra]]\n    92\t  (merge {:id (keyword (name frontend) (name scenario))\n    93\t          :scenario scenario :gates gates :frontends #{frontend}\n    94\t          :frontend frontend :source (sources frontend)\n    95\t          :expected expected :execution :jvm-linked :round 0}\n    96\t         extra))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t(def fixtures\n   100\t  (vec\n   101\t    (concat\n   102\t      (for [f (sort frontends), kind [:named :closure]]\n   103\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"fresh-\" (name kind))) f #{::r1 ::r5}\n   104\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   105\t                  :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true}\n   106\t                 {:callable-kind kind}))\n   107\t      (for [f [:clojure :php :python]]\n   108\t        (fixture :binding f #{::r1} {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   109\t                                     :reason :yang.call/thrown}))\n   110\t      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n   111\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3}\n   112\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   113\t                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n   114\t                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n   115\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   116\t        (fixture :local-reception f #{::r2}\n   117\t                 {:returned true :payload-identical true}))\n   118\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   119\t        (fixture :foreign-reception f #{::r2}\n   120\t                 {:returned true :local-foreign-exception true}))\n   121\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   122\t        (fixture :retained-foreign-lifetime f #{::r2 ::r5}\n   123\t                 {:retained true :local-foreign-exception true\n   124\t                  :transferred true :once true :after false\n   125\t                  :condition-identical true :payload-identical true}))\n   126\t      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n   127\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"saved-protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3 ::r5}\n   128\t                 {:retained true :transferred true :once true :after false\n   129\t                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n   130\t                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n   131\t      (for [f [:clojure :typescript], scenario [:shape-return :shape-throw]]\n   132\t        (fixture scenario f #{::r5}\n   133\t                 (if (= scenario :shape-return)\n   134\t                   {:returned true :payload-identical true}\n   135\t                   {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   136\t                    :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true})))\n   137\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   138\t        (fixture :forged-retention f #{::r5}\n   139\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   140\t                  :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true})))))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(def pair-scenarios\n   144\t  \"Source-pair obligations. Python directions run in Round 0; the other\n   145\t   six directions are authored by the same generators but explicitly await\n   146\t   their frontend rounds. R4's private/public equivalence is a separate\n   147\t   obligation, never inferred from a green pair.\"\n   148\t  {:catch-all #{::r1 ::r2}\n   149\t   :typed-catch #{::r1 ::r2}\n   150\t   :unchanged-rethrow #{::r1 ::r2}\n   151\t   :binding #{::r1}\n   152\t   :finally-replacement #{::r1 ::r2}\n   153\t   :retained-lifetime #{::r1 ::r2}\n   154\t   :round-trip #{::r1 ::r2}\n   155\t   :success-raise-success #{::r1 ::r2}})\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(def pair-matrix\n   159\t  (vec (for [donor (sort frontends), caller (sort frontends)\n   160\t             :when (not= donor caller), [scenario gates] (sort pair-scenarios)\n   161\t             :when (not (and (= scenario :binding) (= donor :typescript)))\n   162\t             :when (not (and (= scenario :finally-replacement) (= caller :clojure)))]\n   163\t         {:id [donor caller scenario] :donor donor :caller caller\n   164\t          :scenario scenario :gates gates :frontends #{donor caller}\n   165\t          :callable-kind :named-export\n   166\t          :catch-surface (case caller :typescript :untyped\n   167\t                               :clojure :single-Exception :local-hierarchy)\n   168\t          :execution (if (#{donor caller} :python)\n   169\t                       :jvm-linked :pending-frontend-rounds)})))\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\t(def pending-obligations\n   173\t  \"Round 0 does not claim the wider acceptance gate. These remain explicit\n   174\t   ledger rows, including facilities the JVM linked kit cannot prove.\"\n   175\t  [{:id :clojure-private-public-equivalence :gates #{::r4}\n   176\t    :frontends #{:clojure} :execution :pending-round-4\n   177\t    :cases #{:caught :uncaught :protocol-rethrow :binding :higher-order}}\n   178\t   {:id :clojure-finally-refusal :gates #{::r4}\n   179\t    :frontends #{:clojure} :execution :preserve-source-refusal}\n   180\t   {:id :suspension-and-recursion :gates #{::r1 ::r2}\n   181\t    :frontends frontends :execution :pending-frontend-rounds}\n   182\t   {:id :host-vm-publication-parity :gates #{::r1 ::r2 ::r3 ::r5}\n   183\t    :frontends frontends :execution :pending-frontend-rounds\n   184\t    :cases #{:node :dart :bundled :task-isolation :custody-refusals}}\n   185\t   {:id :methods-and-callable-objects :gates #{::r1 ::r2 ::r3}\n   186\t    :frontends frontends :execution :pending-frontend-rounds}\n   187\t   {:id :foreign-formatting-and-class-name-forgery :gates #{::r2 ::r5}\n   188\t    :frontends #{:python :php} :execution :pending-frontend-rounds}])\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn ledger-seed\n   192\t  \"Derive obligations per frontend; no hand-maintained claim of acceptance.\"\n   193\t  []\n   194\t  (into (sorted-map)\n   195\t        (for [f (sort frontends)]\n   196\t          [f (into #{} (mapcat :gates)\n   197\t                   (filter #(contains? (:frontends %) f)\n   198\t                           (concat fixtures pair-matrix pending-obligations)))])))\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn open-gates\n   202\t  \"Given `{fixture-or-leg-id :green/:red/:pending}`, derive remaining gates\n   203\t   per frontend. Unreported/pending obligations stay open. A green scalar\n   204\t   observation cannot close a broader portability or lifetime obligation.\"\n   205\t  [statuses]\n   206\t  (into (sorted-map)\n   207\t        (for [f (sort frontends)]\n   208\t          [f (into #{} (mapcat :gates)\n   209\t                   (filter #(and (contains? (:frontends %) f)\n   210\t                                 (not= :green (get statuses (:id %) :pending)))\n   211\t                           (concat fixtures pair-matrix pending-obligations)))])))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
