{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '365,405p'; rg -n 'named|binding-profile|unsupported-binding|invalid-invocation|retained-condition|cell/authentic' test/yang/typescript test/yang/core src/cljc/yang/typescript src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   365\t\n   366\t(defn boundary-call-form\n   367\t  \"An abortive observer of a public entry, as guest code. All arguments are\n   368\t   forms. `options` selects invoke-with when present. A returned envelope\n   369\t   is recorded as :return; only the supplied exit records :raise. Transfer\n   370\t   count and the after-call sentinel live in task cells. No payload is\n   371\t   snapshotted here: assertions must precede rendering.\"\n   372\t  ([callee positional named]\n   373\t   (boundary-call-form callee positional named nil))\n   374\t  ([callee positional named options]\n   375\t   (let [phase (gensym \"phase\")\n   376\t         transfers (gensym \"transfers\")\n   377\t         after (gensym \"after\")\n   378\t         escape (gensym \"escape\")\n   379\t         condition (gensym \"condition\")\n   380\t         returned (gensym \"returned\")\n   381\t         raise (list 'fn [condition]\n   382\t                     (list 'do\n   383\t                           (list 'cell/set! transfers (list '+ 1 (list 'cell/get transfers)))\n   384\t                           (list escape\n   385\t                                 (observation-map-form\n   386\t                                   {:route :raise :condition condition\n   387\t                                    :transfers (list 'cell/get transfers)\n   388\t                                    :after (list 'cell/get after)}))))\n   389\t         invocation (if options\n   390\t                      (list 'yang.call/invoke-with callee positional named raise options)\n   391\t                      (list 'yang.call/invoke callee positio