 `constructor`, a static member named `prototype`, `arguments` in an\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/scope.cljc:489:                (early-error! \"Classes may not have a private field named '#constructor'\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/scope.cljc:494:                (early-error! \"Classes may not have a field or accessor named 'constructor'\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/scope.cljc:498:                (early-error! \"Classes may not have a static property named 'prototype'\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/scope.cljc:782:          ;; a named function expression's own name is immutable\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_module_test.cljc:3:   emitter strips the namespace `js/`, so a definition named like a\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_module_test.cljc:4:   primitive would shadow it inside the module, and a binder named like a\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj:158:   `every-vm=` under the slow guard named `nm`.\"\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/cst_test.clj:115:  (testing \"a default import named type is not a type import\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3540,3605p;4070,4135p'; cat test/yang/core/call_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3540,3605p;4070,4135p'; cat test/yang/core/call_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"  3540\tcross-task interaction continue through `dao.stream`.\n  3541\t\n  3542\t**Transparent calling** means that an admitted callable can be passed,\n  3543\tstored, returned, and invoked by any conforming frontend without a\n  3544\thandwritten language-pair wrapper. It does not mean every foreign value\n  3545\tsatisfies every source operation. Invocation, name visibility, and value\n  3546\tinterpretation are distinct obligations.\n  3547\t\n  3548\tThe convention covers ordinary source calls and supported callable\n  3549\tobjects, including higher-order calls. It does not make macros runtime\n  3550\tfunctions, grant JavaScript `[[Construct]]`, turn a generator into an\n  3551\tordinary returning function, or add a source feature a frontend refuses.\n  3552\tConstructors and asynchronous operations keep their declared source\n  3553\tsemantics; ordinary callability does not imply either capability.\n  3554\t\n  3555\t#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\n  3556\t\n  3557\tKeep the callable's existing identity and source-specific data. Add the\n  3558\tcommon entry beside its private code and metadata:\n  3559\t\n  3560\t```clojure\n  3561\t;; Illustrative contents of one task-owned Python function cell.\n  3562\t;; `entry` and `body-code` are live Yin closures, not literal AST maps.\n  3563\t{:yang.call/entry entry\n  3564\t :py/type :function\n  3565\t :spec parameter-spec\n  3566\t :defaults defaults\n  3567\t :code body-code}\n  3568\t```\n  3569\t\n  3570\tThe existing `:code` field is not the shared entry: its signature differs\n  3571\tbetween preludes. It may remain private. Cross-language callers must not\n  3572\tinspect it or extract it to bypass the entry.\n  3573\t\n  3574\tA cell-backed callable stores the entry in its cell contents. An\n  3575\timmutable callable descriptor, such as a bound method, may carry it\n  3576\tdirectly in its map. The common prelude projects the entry structurally:\n  3577\tread an existing sealed cell reference through `cell/get`, or inspect\n  3578\tthe immutable descriptor, then obtain `:yang.call/entry`. A\n  3579\tcell-ref-shaped map is dereferenced only when the heap authenticates it\n  3580\t(`cell/authentic?`, section 8.10.12); an unauthenticated shape projects\n  3581\tto itself and follows the ordinary descriptor rules, so data imitating\n  3582\tthe reference language stays data. The projection must not\n  3583\tdispatch on `:py/type`, `:js/type`, `:php/type`, language names, or a\n  3584\tregistry of languages.\n  3585\t\n  3586\tAn admitted callable is a runtime cell/descriptor constructed or exposed\n  3587\tby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\n  3588\tconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\n  3589\tsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\n  3590\tdictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\n  3591\tspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\n  3592\tprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\n  3593\tproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\n  3594\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n  3595\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n  3596\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n  3597\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n  3598\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n  3599\t\n  3600\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n  3601\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n  3602\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n  3603\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n  3604\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n  3605\tA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\n  4070\t  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\n  4071\t- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\n  4072\t  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\n  4073\t  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\n  4074\t  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\n  4075\t\n  4076\tReport callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\n  4077\tcoverage as an explicit host-by-VM matrix, refusals, and remaining gaps\n  4078\tper frontend revision. A scalar example or common UAST grammar alone\n  4079\tdoes not establish conformance.\n  4080\t\n  4081\t#### 8.10.12 Cell-reference call routing and authenticity\n  4082\t\n  4083\tRuling of record (2026-11-04, owner-approved). A cross-language\n  4084\treference is a cell-ref map the VM issues (`{:type :cell-ref :id\n  4085\t:cell-N :seal s}`). In Clojure a map is callable, so the call lowering\n  4086\tmust route a callee between reference semantics and data semantics.\n  4087\tThree rounds routed by value shape at call time (key presence,\n  4088\texact shape, minted-id language) and each left the same defect class:\n  4089\tinnocent data whose shape imitates the reference language aborted at\n  4090\t`cell/get` instead of answering as data. The defect is structural — a\n  4091\tgenuine reference and a perfect imitation are field-identical maps,\n  4092\tand the distinguishing fact (did the heap issue this?) is not in the\n  4093\tvalue. It is in the heap. Only the issuer can answer.\n  4094\t\n  4095\t- **Vocabulary.** The `cell` host module's published effect vocabulary\n  4096\t  is `{new, get, set!, authentic?}`. `cell/authentic?` is a pure\n  4097\t  query: the engine answers the same heap+seal predicate `check-ref!`\n  4098\t  consults, as a boolean, non-fatally, state unchanged. The engine\n  4099\t  learns no frontend semantics; it answers a generic fact about its\n  4100\t  own state (the no-collapse invariant holds — the invoke-vs-lookup\n  4101\t  decision remains in compiled guest code).\n  4102\t- **Routing asks the heap, never the shape.** Where the callee value\n  4103\t  has the cell-ref shape, compiled code consults `cell/authentic?`:\n  4104\t  authentic → the reference path (`cell/get` plus the existing\n  4105\t  admission/apply machinery); not authentic → ordinary data semantics\n  4106\t  (map lookup). The shape remains a cheap pre-filter for WHEN to ask;\n  4107\t  it never decides meaning. The shared descriptor projection\n  4108\t  (`yang.call/_descriptor`) consults the same way.\n  4109\t- **Interim asymmetry (agreed across the four seats).** The frontend\n  4110\t  kind predicates that route on a `:type :cell-ref` tag before\n  4111\t  dereferencing — TypeScript's `js/cell?` and Python's `py/cell?` —\n  4112\t  still test SHAPE alone at this landing; their owning seats sweep\n  4113\t  them onto `cell/authentic?` in-lane after this merge (TypeScript:\n  4114\t  the `typeof` path and member-call lowering; Python: the three deref\n  4115\t  sites — `py/content-type`, type resolution, `py/eq-objects`). Until\n  4116\t  those sweeps land, a map imitating the reference language is data\n  4117\t  at Clojure positions and at the shared descriptor projection, but\n  4118\t  can still abort at the unswept frontend predicates. Nothing\n  4119\t  currently-correct changes behavior (the widening property holds);\n  4120\t  all-frontends consistency completes at the owning seats' landings.\n  4121\t- **Authentication is not authorization.** An authentic reference\n  4122\t  whose cell lacks an admitted callable entry is not callable; the\n  4123\t  existing not-callable refusal stands. Explicit dereference at a\n  4124\t  reference position (`cell/get`) likewise keeps the strict\n  4125\t  validation boundary — the data fallback lives in call routing.\n  4126\t- **Bearer policy.** An exact copy of a valid reference retains\n  4127\t  bearer behavior: it authenticates, therefore it resolves. No\n  4128\t  construction-history promises are made for identical values. A\n  4129\t  program wanting such a map's fields as data uses explicit lookup at\n  4130\t  a data position.\n  4131\t- **Bag clarification.** A reference stored in data remains a\n  4132\t  reference: storage changes nothing about the value, and what\n  4133\t  decides is the authentication query at the eventual call, not where\n  4134\t  the callee travelled. Equality survives while callability follows\n  4135\t  the heap's answer.\n(ns yang.core.call-test\n  \"Synthetic guest proof for the language-neutral calling runtime.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def ^:private registry\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      data/register-data-module))\n\n\n(def ^:private opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\n   :primitives vm/primitives\n   :modules registry})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(def ^:private runners\n  {:ast-walker (fn [ast] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast))\n   :semantic (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                          (vm/ast->datoms ast))))\n   :stack (fn [ast]\n            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                      (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))\n   :register (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n                         (derive/register-image\n                           (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                         (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\n\n\n(defn- run-everywhere\n  [emitter form]\n  (let [ast (u/mark-tails (u/then emitter (u/sexp->uast form)))]\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [[engine run]] [engine (vm/value (run ast))]))\n          runners)))\n\n\n(deftest base-validation-and-construction-test\n  (testing \"required fields, ordered names, duplicate names and receiver presence\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named [[\"x\" 1] [\"x\" 2]]\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit\n                            :yang.call/receiver nil})))))\n    (is (every? false?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named [[1 :bad]]\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit})))))\n    (is (every? false?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional nil\n                            :yang.call/named []\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit}))))))\n  (testing \"invocation-with retains optional fields and cannot replace core fields\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [record\n                               (yang.call/invocation-with\n                                 :callee [] [] :exit\n                                 {:yang.call/receiver nil\n                                  :yang.call/callee :substitute})]\n                           (if (= :callee (get record :yang.call/callee))\n                             (if (data/contains? record :yang.call/receiver)\n                               (nil? (get record :yang.call/receiver))\n                               false)\n                             false))))))))\n\n\n(deftest entry-and-invocation-test\n  (testing \"descriptor entry, eligibility, original identity and unchanged result\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [callee {:opaque [1 2]}\n                               descriptor\n                               (assoc {}\n                                      :yang.call/entry\n                                      (fn [inv]\n                                        (get inv :yang.call/callee)))]\n                           (yang.call/eligible? descriptor))))))\n    (let [payload [1 2]]\n      (is (every? #(= payload %)\n                  (vals (run-everywhere\n                          call/uast\n                          '(let [callee (assoc {} :opaque [1 2])\n                                 descriptor\n                                 (assoc callee\n                                        :yang.call/entry\n                                        (fn [inv]\n                                          (get (get inv :yang.call/callee)\n                                               :opaque)))]\n                             (yang.call/invoke descriptor [] []\n                                               (fn [condition]\n                                                 condition)))))))))\n  (testing \"cell-backed entry lookup and an ineligible descriptor\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [descriptor\n                               (cell/new\n                                 (assoc {}\n                                        :yang.call/entry\n                                        (fn [inv] :called)))\n                               ineligible\n                               (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/entry\n                                             (fn [inv] :wrong))\n                                      :yang.call/eligible?\n                                      (fn [callee] false))\n                               called\n                               (yang.call/invoke\n                                 descriptor [] []\n                                 (fn [condition] condition))\n                               result\n                               (yang.call/invoke\n                                 ineligible [] []\n                                 (fn [condition] condition))]\n                           (if (= :called called)\n                             (= :yang.call/not-callable\n                                (get result :yang.call/reason))\n                             false))))))))\n\n\n(deftest conditions-and-transfer-test\n  (testing \"throwing wraps condition-shaped data; normal return remains data\"\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(let [payload {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                                        :yang.call/value :inner}\n                               result (yang.call/thrown payload)]\n                           (if (= payload (get result :yang.call/value))\n                             (= :yang.call/thrown\n                                (get result :yang.call/reason))\n                             false)))))))\n  (testing \"transfer applies the supplied exit once\"\n    (is (every? #(= {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n                     :yang.call/data {:callee :value}\n                     :seen true}\n                    %)\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/uast\n                        '(yang.call/transfer\n                           (fn [condition]\n                             (assoc condition :seen true))\n                           (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                                {:callee :value})))))))\n  (testing \"bundled and linked emitters use the same definition source\"\n    (is (= call/module-uast\n           (u/annotate-call-sites\n             (core/module-tree\n               (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n                                        [] call/definitions)\n               []))))\n    (is (= call/module-exports\n           (:exports (call/module-spec registry))))\n    (is (= call/host-names\n           (set (filter namespace\n                        (keys (:primitives (call/module-spec registry)))))))\n    (is (every? true?\n                (vals (run-everywhere\n                        call/module-uast\n                        '(valid-invocation?\n                           {:yang.call/callee :f\n                            :yang.call/positional []\n                            :yang.call/named []\n                            :yang.call/raise :exit})))))))\n\n\n(deftest cross-frontend-callable-identity-fixture-test\n  (testing \"a stored PHP function crosses a TS entry, is called, and stays same-cell\"\n    (let [results (run-everywhere\n                    call/uast\n                    '(let [php-function\n                           (cell/new\n                             (assoc {:php/type :function}\n                                    :yang.call/entry\n                                    (fn [invocation]\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/callee))))\n                           stored (cell/new php-function)\n                           original (cell/get stored)\n                           typescript-relay\n                           (assoc {}\n                                  :yang.call/entry\n                                  (fn [invocation]\n                                    (yang.call/invoke\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/receiver)\n                                      [] []\n                                      (get invocation :yang.call/raise))))\n                           returned\n                           (yang.call/invoke-with\n                             typescript-relay [] []\n                             (fn [condition] condition)\n                             (assoc {} :yang.call/receiver original))]\n                       (if (= original returned) :same :different)))]\n      (is (every? #{:same} (vals results))\n          (pr-str results))))\n  (testing \"Python calls a TS entry, receives a callback, then calls the PHP entry\"\n    (let [results\n          (run-everywhere\n            call/uast\n            '(let [php-function\n                   (cell/new\n                     (assoc {:php/type :function}\n                            :yang.call/entry\n                            (fn [invocation]\n                              (get invocation :yang.call/callee))))\n                   python-function (cell/new {:py/type :function})\n                   typescript-function\n                   (assoc {:js/type :function}\n                          :yang.call/entry\n                          (fn [invocation]\n                            (yang.call/invoke\n                              python-function [php-function] []\n                              (get invocation :yang.call/raise))))\n                   _ (cell/set!\n                       python-function\n                       (assoc (cell/get python-function)\n                              :yang.call/entry\n                              (fn [invocation]\n                                (if (= 0 (data/count\n                                           (get invocation :yang.call/positional)))\n                                  (yang.call/invoke\n                                    typescript-function [] []\n                                    (get invocation :yang.call/raise))\n                                  (yang.call/invoke\n                                    php-function [] []\n                                    (get invocation :yang.call/raise))))))\n                   returned\n                   (yang.call/invoke\n                     python-function [] [] (fn [condition] condition))]\n               (if (= php-function returned) :same :different)))]\n      (is (every? #{:same} (vals results))\n          (pr-str results)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
