ance-gap.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"ref: refs/heads/f1-importers-diagnosis-r2\\\\n   618\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   619\\\\t;;\\\\n   620\\\\t;; Opted in with `:outcomes true` beside the argument-vector convention. Every\\\\n   621\\\\t;; guest function then returns an outcome, a tagged two-element vector:\\\\n   622\\\\t;;\\\\n   623\\\\t;;   [:yin.k/ok value]       success; a LaTTe [:ok ...] stays an ordinary value\\\\n   624\\\\t;;   [:yin.k/error data]     failure; never a truthy return, only ever consumed\\\\n   625\\\\t;;                           by a call-site test or the harness boundary\\\\n   626\\\\t;;\\\\n   627\\\\t;; Lowering is a source-to-source pass over one function body, run before the\\\\n   628\\\\t;; ordinary compile. A tail form returns an outcome: a value is wrapped,\\\\n   629\\\\t;; and a source call is admitted before invoking the common entry. Generated\\\\n   630\\\\t;; entries can forward a private body's outcome directly in tail position;\\\\n   631\\\\t;; public entries convert value/raise through the caller bridge. This keeps\\\\n   632\\\\t;; named and mutual tail chains at constant depth. `throw` becomes the error\\\\n   633\\\\t;; outcome. A may-fail form in operand position is the early return pattern:\\\\n   634\\\\t;;\\\\n   635\\\\t;;   (let [o <outcome>] (if (error? o) o <rest of the function with (payload o)>))\\\\n   636\\\\t;;\\\\n   637\\\\t;; The failing branch returns the outcome in tail position. `ex-info` becomes\\\\n   638\\\\t;; a portable map under namespaced keys. A native primitive returns a raw\\\\n   639\\\\t;; value, except an adapted one (`:adapters`, source symbol to adapter symbol),\\\\n   640\\\\t;; whose host adapter already returns an outcome. Generated names carry the\\\\n   641\\\\t;; reserved `dsg__` prefix and bind through the internal `dsg__let`, which\\\\n   642\\\\t;; skips the user-binder check; the program pre-pa