 1367\\\\t          ;; A callee carrying a call entry is convention territory whether it\\\\n  1368\\\\t          ;; admits or forges one, so admission rules it. Everything else is a\\\\n  1369\\\\t          ;; data-side invocation - a collection lookup or a raw closure call -\\\\n  1370\\\\t          ;; and the guest library's invoker owns those semantics. The invoker\\\\n  1371\\\\t          ;; is itself a published descriptor, so it is reached the same way\\\\n  1372\\\\t          ;; any guest callee is; its raise escapes to a capture of this site\\\\n  1373\\\\t          ;; and the resumed pass materializes the error outcome here.\\\\n  1374\\\\t          value-call (u/app\\\\n  1375\\\\t                       (u/lam ['dsg__raise_escape]\\\\n  1376\\\\t                              (u/if-node\\\\n  1377\\\\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/callable?) (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape))\\\\n  1378\\\\t                                (u/let1\\\\n  1379\\\\t                                  (symbol (str reserved-prefix \\\\\\\"invoker_result\\\\\\\"))\\\\n  1380\\\\t                                  (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke)\\\\n  1381\\\\t                                         (u/v 'invoke-value)\\\\n  1382\\\\t                                         (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/v callee) (u/v arguments))\\\\n  1383\\\\t                                         (u/lit [])\\\\n  1384\\\\t                                         (u/lam [condition]\\\\n  1385\\\\t                                                (assoc (u/app (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape)\\\\n  1386\\\\t                                                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\\\\n  1387\\\\t                                                                     (u/lit :clj/escape-token) (u/v 'dsg__call_token)\\\\n  1388\\\\t                                                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome) condition->outcome))\\\\n  1389\\\\t                     