ils published)\\\\n  1150\\\\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\\\\n  1151\\\\t\\\\n  1152\\\\t\\\\n  1153\\\\t(defn- compile-call-descriptor\\\\n  1154\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Publish a private body through a canonical constructor-created entry.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  1155\\\\t  [body-ast tail?]\\\\n  1156\\\\t  (admit-call-descriptor\\\\n  1157\\\\t    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\\\\n  1158\\\\t           (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_entry) body-ast)\\\\n  1159\\\\t           (u/lit :clj/type) (u/lit :function)\\\\n  1160\\\\t           (u/lit :clj/outcomes?) (u/lit true))\\\\n  1161\\\\t    tail?))\\\\n  1162\\\\t\\\\n  1163\\\\t\\\\n  1164\\\\t(defn- compile-av-fn\\\\n  1165\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\\\\n  1238\\\\t  [env operator]\\\\n  1239\\\\t  (and (outcomes? env)\\\\n  1240\\\\t       (symbol? operator)\\\\n  1241\\\\t       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\\\\n  1242\\\\t       (contains? (::defined-fns env) operator)))\\\\n  1243\\\\t\\\\n  1244\\\\t\\\\n  1245\\\\t(defn- cell-ref-shaped-node\\\\n  1246\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UAST test that the callee node could be a cell reference the\\\\n  1247\\\\t   VM issued: `:type :cell-ref` with the `:id` and `:seal` every\\\\n  1248\\\\t   issued reference carries, no other entries, a seal of the issued\\\\n  1249\\\\t   form (a 64-character string), and an `:id` in the engine's heap\\\\n  1250\\\\t   id language — every cell id is a `:cell-N` keyword (engine\\\\n  1251\\\\t   `gen-id` mints them all from one counter), so an `:id` that is\\\\n  1252\\\\t   not such a keyword names no cell the task could ever have\\\\n  1253\\\\t   minted and the map is data, whatever its other entries spell.\\\\n  1254\\\\t   A map that fails this test is never dereferenced: it routes to\\\\n  1255\\\\t   ordinary map invocation, which grants no cell capability. A map\\\\n  1256\\\\t   that passes it is a dereference *candidate*, not a proven\\\\n  1257\\\\